{
  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "No supported optimization applies to this workflow without weakening coverage or relying on unsupported assumptions. The workflow already caches the local Maven repository (~/.m2/repository) with a key keyed on java-version, job context, and hashFiles('**/pom.xml'), so P-LIT-GHA-CACHE (dependency download caching) is contraindicated because an equivalent cache already exists. P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT and P-LIT-HISTORY-TIMEOUT require representative successful-duration history, but the CI history shows no completed runs, so an evidence-based timeout cannot be set and an arbitrary limit risks breaking valid slow runs. P-LIT-FAIL-FAST and P-LIT-FAILED-JOB-FIRST need a matrix or multiple jobs with dispensable/reorderable outcomes; this workflow has a single job. P-LIT-FAIL-SCHEDULE and P-LIT-IDLE-SCHEDULE apply to scheduled workflows, but this is a reusable workflow_call with no schedule. The Bazel parallelism/incremental-cache patterns do not apply because the project builds with Maven, not Bazel. Test selection/prioritization patterns do not apply because the job runs a Docker/Spark integration rather than a unit-test suite with required checks to preserve. Change-path filtering, workflow skipping, distributed caching, environment reuse, unused-output removal, and configuration reuse all lack established prerequisites in this repository and could alter required-check semantics.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-GHA-CACHE", "P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT", "P-LIT-FAIL-FAST", "P-LIT-IDLE-SCHEDULE", "P-LIT-BAZEL-PARALLEL"]
}
